cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Queyi datasets, real-world benchmark, or tooling, please cite this repository."
title: "Queyi: Failure-Driven Verifier Evolution for C++ Defect Detection (datasets, benchmark, and tooling)"
abstract: >-
  Queyi is a research line and reproducible toolchain for failure-driven evolution of
  C++ defect detector portfolios: four-state verdicts (pass/fail/unknown/contradict),
  an append-only ledger with Merkle integrity, and a deterministic portfolio operator E
  scored by failure coverage / novelty / cost / redundancy. This repository also hosts
  (a) a 1,147-sample x 8-asset frozen detection matrix, and (b) a real-world benchmark of
  reconstructed C++ defects with traceable CVE/issue/commit provenance and NVD-verified
  metadata.
